-- title:
--   Chart images in the descended unramified quotient: open and covering
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower with its unramified layer, and the hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   *Base ring.* A prime $r$; a characteristic-zero commutative domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi \in \mathcal O$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $(\pi)$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue cardinality $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ (`hres`) and the unramifiedness condition $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   *Unramified coefficient ring.* A characteristic-zero commutative domain $Onr$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ of $Onr$, subject to: $(\pi Onr)$-adic completeness (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_max`), the condition that every $x \in Onr$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), the condition that every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   *Determinant valuation.* A homomorphism $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g)$ equals $n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   *Arithmetic group data.* A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma \le G$, with: `hcent`, asserting the existence of $z \in \Gamma$ whose image $\sigma z$ is a scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ and satisfies $vdet(\sigma z) = 2$; `hodd`, asserting the existence of $w \in \Gamma$ with $vdet(\sigma w) = 1$; and a subgroup $\Gamma' \le G$ specified by `hΓ'` as the set of $x \in \Gamma$ with $vdet(\sigma x)$ even. Further, a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with $\rho g$ the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`), and, for the action of $\rho(\Gamma')$ on the vertex set [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) (lattices up to homothety), finiteness of every vertex stabiliser (`hdisc`) and the existence of a finite set of vertices meeting every orbit (`hcocpt`). The matrix $g_1$ is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`).
--
--   *Mumford tower.* A subgroup $N \le \rho(\Gamma')$ with $N \cap \rho(\Gamma)$ normal in $\rho(\Gamma)$ (`hNnorm`) and of nonzero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`), together with a `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N` denoted $DM$: schemes $Z_n$ with structure morphisms $zb_n$ to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transition maps $zt_n$ forming a cartesian, proper, flat tower admitting affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, plus a family of maps $DM.q$ attaching to a Deligne datum over an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$ a $B$-point of $Z_n$, natural, compatible with the tower and invariant under pullback along elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ whose class lies in $N$.
--
--   *Twisted tower.* Schemes $X_n$ (in universe $0$) with morphisms $xb_n$ to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $xt_n$, a finite group $G_2$ acting by automorphisms $a_n$, projections $pr_{1,n} : X_n \to Z_n$ and $pr_{2,n}$ to the spectrum of the reduction modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ of the fixed ring $\mathrm{eq}(Fr \circ Fr, \mathrm{id})$ of the square of $Fr$, a surjection $\theta : \Gamma \to G_2$ and automorphisms $Fr_{2,n}$ of those reductions. The hypotheses on these data are: `hcart` (the tower is cartesian over the base reductions), `hproper` and `hflat` (each $xb_n$ is proper and flat), `haff` (finite subsets of $X_n$ lie in affine opens), `ha_over` and `ha_xt` ($G_2$ acts over the base and compatibly with the transitions), `hX` (each $X_n$ is the fibre product of $Z_n$ with the spectrum of the reduced fixed ring), `hxb`, `hxt₁`, `hxt₂` (compatibility of the two projections with the base morphisms and the transition maps), `hθker` ($\theta\gamma = 1$ if and only if $\rho\gamma \in N$), `hFr₂` ($Fr_{2,n}$ is induced by $Fr$ on the fixed ring), `ha_pr₂` (the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on $pr_{2,n}$ through $Fr_{2,n}^{-vdet(\sigma\gamma)}$), and `ha_pr₁` (the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ transports the point of $Z_n$ attached to a Deligne datum $P$ to the one attached to any $P'$ which is the pullback of $P$ along $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$).
--
--   *Formal quotient.* A `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a` denoted $DQ$: schemes $Y_n$ with base morphisms $yb_n$, transitions $yt_n$ forming a cartesian proper flat tower, and $G_2$-invariant maps $p_n : X_n \to Y_n$ which are finite, surjective, cartesian over the transitions, locally epimorphic and satisfy the stated local universal property. Attached to it is a family of maps $q$ sending a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $Onr \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (for $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$) to a $B$-point of $Y_n$, subject to `hqdef` (the point $q$ is the composite with $p_n$ of any point of $X_n$ whose two projections are the given Deligne datum and the given algebra homomorphism), `hqover` (compatibility with the structure morphisms), `hqnat` (naturality in $B$), `hqyt` (compatibility with the transitions) and `hqinv` (invariance under the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` of $\sigma\gamma$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma$, i.e. Frobenius twisting by $-vdet(\sigma\gamma)$ on the first component together with pullback of the Deligne datum along $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$).
--
--   *Unramified layer.* A `MumfordTower.NrPresentation` denoted $Pr$, for the above data and for the subgroup $\theta(\Gamma' \cap \Gamma)$ of $G_2$: schemes $X'_n$ over $Onr/\pi^{n+1}$ with transitions $xt'_n$, a $G_2$-action $a'_n$, morphisms $qX_n : X'_n \to X_n$ exhibiting $X'_n$ as the base change of $X_n$ along $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1} \to Onr/\pi^{n+1}$, all compatibilities of $qX$ with the transitions and with the actions, and charts $\kappa'_{h,n}$, indexed by $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, from the spectrum of the reduction modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ of the chart ring `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` to $X'_n$, with the chart properties recorded in that structure. Finally a `TowerQuotientDatum Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) Pr.X' Pr.xb' Pr.xt' G₂ Pr.a'` denoted $D'$, with quotient maps $p'_n : X'_n \to D'.Y_n$, together with morphisms $rY_n : D'.Y_n \to DQ.Y_n$ such that $rY_n$ exhibits $D'.Y_n$ as the base change of $DQ.Y_n$ along $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1} \to Onr/\pi^{n+1}$ (`hrY`), such that $p'_n$ followed by $rY_n$ equals $qX_n$ followed by $p_n$ (`hrY_p`), and such that $D'.yt_n$ followed by $rY_{n+1}$ equals $rY_n$ followed by $DQ.yt_n$ (`hrY_yt`).
--
--   The conclusion is a conjunction of two statements about the composites $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $p'_n$, as maps of the underlying topological spaces. First: for every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $n \in \mathbb N$, the range of the underlying map of $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $p'_n$ is an open subset of $D'.Y_n$. Second: for every $n \in \mathbb N$, the union over all $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ of these ranges is the whole of $D'.Y_n$.
--
--   This records that the charts of the unramified layer, pushed down to the formal quotient, give an open covering of each layer $D'.Y_n$ of the quotient tower; it is the topological input needed before gluing the chart descriptions into a description of the quotient. It is cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts), and its proof uses the orbit description of the fibres of a tower quotient map, [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.p_base_eq_iff_and_preimage_image_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.p_base_eq_iff_and_preimage_image_eq).
